|~ What is declared under `::fail`, the step `!|` runs on an error
   alone: its refusals. ~|

:fail/construct
  |~~ The step `!| step` from the quote of its step. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:fail/PayloadNotQuoteError
  |~~ The payload of `::fail` is the quote of the step it wraps.

      ~(
        42 | tag ::fail
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::fail/PayloadNotQuoteError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

:fail/ReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The `::fail` prints as text that reads back as another step: it
      wraps one step, and a pipeline under `!|` is written as a
      group.

      ~(
        ~(a | b) | tag ::fail
        !| [type /printed]
        |  eq [::fail/ReadBackDiffersError "!| a | b"]
       )
  ~~|
